description.narrative:
Denmark supports the ICRC with a non-earmarked core contribution towards their global, inter-regional humanitarian response in conflict settings of developing and fragile countries. The objective is protection and humanitarian assistance to the most vulnerable as well as prevention and reduction of violence and conflict.
Denmark contributes to the following results:
1. Protection and delivery of essential services to people affected by conflict;
2. Promotion and compliance with International Humanitarian Law;
3. Synergies between humanitarian and development efforts / Sustainable Humanitarian Impact;
4. Climate and conflict;
5. Enhanced organisational efficiency and effectiveness of the ICRC.
